# Static

Serving a frontend bundle off disk, written entirely in LOGOS over the
`readBytes` builtin and `http.lg`'s `bytesResponse`/`notFound`. Three helpers:
`contentTypeFor` maps a path's extension to its MIME type, `fileResponse` reads
a file's raw bytes and answers with that type, and `staticUnder` serves a file
rooted at a directory behind a HARD path-traversal guard — any `..` segment in
the requested path is refused with a 404 before a single byte reaches disk, so a
crafted `../../etc/passwd` can never climb above the served root.

## Note
The MIME type for `path`, chosen by its file extension (matched case-insensitively so a wire path in any casing resolves the same).

An unknown or absent extension is `application/octet-stream` — the generic
binary type, never a guess.
## To contentTypeFor (path: Text) -> Text:
    Let p be lower(path).
    If endsWith(p, ".html") is equal to true:
        Return "text/html; charset=utf-8".
    If endsWith(p, ".htm") is equal to true:
        Return "text/html; charset=utf-8".
    If endsWith(p, ".js") is equal to true:
        Return "text/javascript".
    If endsWith(p, ".mjs") is equal to true:
        Return "text/javascript".
    If endsWith(p, ".wasm") is equal to true:
        Return "application/wasm".
    If endsWith(p, ".css") is equal to true:
        Return "text/css; charset=utf-8".
    If endsWith(p, ".svg") is equal to true:
        Return "image/svg+xml".
    If endsWith(p, ".xml") is equal to true:
        Return "application/xml".
    If endsWith(p, ".png") is equal to true:
        Return "image/png".
    If endsWith(p, ".jpg") is equal to true:
        Return "image/jpeg".
    If endsWith(p, ".jpeg") is equal to true:
        Return "image/jpeg".
    If endsWith(p, ".gif") is equal to true:
        Return "image/gif".
    If endsWith(p, ".webp") is equal to true:
        Return "image/webp".
    If endsWith(p, ".json") is equal to true:
        Return "application/json".
    If endsWith(p, ".txt") is equal to true:
        Return "text/plain; charset=utf-8".
    If endsWith(p, ".ico") is equal to true:
        Return "image/x-icon".
    If endsWith(p, ".woff") is equal to true:
        Return "font/woff".
    If endsWith(p, ".woff2") is equal to true:
        Return "font/woff2".
    If endsWith(p, ".pdf") is equal to true:
        Return "application/pdf".
    Return "application/octet-stream".

## Note
A 200 OK response carrying the raw bytes of the file at `path`, typed by its extension through `contentTypeFor`.

This is the byte-exact serving path — the file is delivered verbatim
(`bytesResponse` puts the bytes in the response's `bytes` field and leaves the
text `body` empty), so a `.wasm` or `.png` is never mangled by a text round-
trip. A MISSING file is a 404, never a trap: `tryReadBytes` answers a `Result`,
so the read either hands over the bytes or says why it could not.

This used to probe with the recoverable `read` first and then call the aborting
`readBytes`, because there was no total byte reader. That cost two things on the
hot path of every asset a site serves: a RACE — a file removed between the probe
and the read aborted the whole server rather than the request — and TWICE THE
WORK, since the probe fully decoded the file as lossy UTF-8, a String the size of
the file, only to look at its Ok/Err verdict and throw it away.
## To fileResponse (path: Text) -> Response:
    Inspect tryReadBytes(path):
        When Ok (payload):
            Return bytesResponse(contentTypeFor(path), payload).
        When Err (why):
            Return notFound().

## Note
True when `path` contains a `..` segment — the directory-traversal guard.

The path is split on `/` and each segment tested for exact equality with `..`,
so a leading (`../x`), interior (`a/../b`), or climbing (`a/../../x`) traversal
is all caught. A bare `..`, or a `..` amid otherwise-benign names, is caught
too. Prefix tricks like `..foo` are NOT a traversal (they name a real file) and
pass.
## To hasTraversal (path: Text) -> Bool:
    Let segs be split(path, "/").
    Repeat for seg in segs:
        If seg is equal to "..":
            Return true.
    Return false.

## Note
Serves the file at `path` rooted under `dir`, behind the path-traversal guard.

A `path` carrying any `..` segment is refused with `notFound()` (404) BEFORE the
file layer is touched — the security contract. A safe path is joined under the
root (`dir/path`); a leading `/` on the request path (handlers see
`/index.html`, not `index.html`) is stripped first so the join never doubles the
separator. The resolved file is served byte-exact through `fileResponse`.
Percent-decoding is the wire parser's job (the handler already sees a decoded
path); this guard is the last line of defence on the decoded value.
## To staticUnder (dir: Text) and (path: Text) -> Response:
    If hasTraversal(path) is equal to true:
        Return notFound().
    Let rel be removePrefix(path, "/").
    Let full be "{dir}/{rel}".
    Return fileResponse(full).
